B.QU=new A.fM(8,"Maneshayh","West","Shevo","Maneshayh represents refinement, restraint, message integration, disciplined communication, and harmonized understanding.","Integrator represents synthesis, alignment, reconciliation, coherence-building, and the joining of separate parts into a working whole.","Maneshayh and Integrator align as the harmonizing intelligence of the cycle: many messages are refined into one coherent pattern.","Progression","Integrator")
B.QV=new A.fM(13,"Ber\xfawkah","Leap / Intercalary","Beryl","Ber\xfawkah represents blessing, transition, systemic alignment, and the balancing of the solar-lunar offset.","An extra-cyclical adjustment node ensuring synchronization across multi-year cycles.","Ber\xfawkah serves as the intercalary transition: a periodic adjustment phase resetting the alignment between lunar months and solar years.","Leap","None / Intercalary")
B.QW=new A.fM(4,"RA\xfawaben","South","Nofech","RA\xfawaben represents seeing, perception, revelation, foundations, hidden structure, and the opening of inner sight.","Visionary represents future-sight, pattern projection, imaginative perception, and the ability to see beyond the immediately visible.","RA\xfawaben and Visionary align as the eye of the cycle: the capacity to perceive what is forming beneath the surface.","Development","Visionary")
B.QX=new A.fM(6,"Gad","South","Yahalom","Gad represents speech, words, articulation, wisdom expressed through the mouth, and manifestation through utterance.","Speaker represents expression, declaration, verbalization, communication, and the conversion of inner structure into outward signal.","Gad and Speaker align as the voice of the cycle: what has been seen and heard now becomes articulated.","Development","Speaker")
B.QY=new A.fM(3,"Zeb\xfawlan","East","Bareketh","Zeb\xfawlan represents knowledge exchange, movement between domains, fruitful labor, extension, and circulation.","Connector represents relational linkage, transmission, exchange, network formation, and bridging between separated elements.","Zeb\xfawlan and Connector align as the movement of knowledge into relationship, trade, expression, and fruitful contact.","Initiation","Connector")
B.QZ=new A.fM(5,"Shamo\xfann","South","Sappir","Shamo\xfann represents hearing, reception, obedience to signal, understanding through listening, and inward resonance.","Hearer represents receptive intelligence, attunement, signal detection, listening, and resonance awareness.","Shamo\xfann and Hearer align as the receptive chamber of the cycle: the ability to hear what time is communicating.","Development","Hearer")
B.R_=new A.fM(1,"Yah\xfadah","East","Odem","Yah\xfadah represents activation, kingship, emergence, first illumination, and the bringing of structure into visible form.","Spark represents ignition, beginning, first movement, energetic emergence, and the initiation of a new temporal cycle.","Yah\xfadah and Spark align as the first movement of the cycle: the moment where light, will, identity, and temporal action begin.","Initiation","Spark")
B.R0=new A.fM(12,"Nephetli","North","Yashpheh","Nephetli represents culmination, wisdom synthesis, transmission, perfected sayings, completion, and the drawing out of strength.","Inspirer represents uplift, transmission, renewal of vision, final synthesis, and the release of completed meaning into the next cycle.","Nephetli and Inspirer align as the completing breath of the cycle: wisdom is drawn out, transmitted, and prepared to become new initiation.","Completion","Inspirer")
B.R1=new A.fM(11,"Ayshshur","North","Shoham","Ayshshur represents establishment, maturity, completion of instruction, stability, recompense, and settled capability.","Harmonizer represents balance, stabilization, agreement, relational coherence, and the restoration of internal and external equilibrium.","Ayshshur and Harmonizer align as the stabilizing power of the cycle: what has been tested is matured into balance.","Completion","Harmonizer")
B.R2=new A.fM(7,"Aparryim","West","Leshem","Aparryim represents habitation, cultivation, enclosure, covering, settlement, growth, and the ordering of space.","Architect represents structure, design, system-building, framework creation, and the making of inhabitable order.","Aparryim and Architect align as the builder of the cycle: the stage where resonance becomes structure.","Progression","Architect")
B.R3=new A.fM(9,"Beniyman","West","Achlamah","Beniyman represents return, renewal, chambers, restoration, right-hand action, and the reorganization of movement through cycles.","Strategist represents planning, orientation, sequencing, adaptive movement, and purposeful navigation through complexity.","Beniyman and Strategist align as the tactical intelligence of the cycle: return and renewal become directed movement.","Progression","Strategist")
B.R4=new A.fM(2,"Yishshakkar","East","Pitdah","Yishshakkar represents discernment of cycles, assembled knowledge, timing, counting, ordering, and recognition of pattern.","Analyst represents observation, distinction, classification, measurement, and structural understanding.","Yishshakkar and Analyst align as the intelligence that reads the structure of time and recognizes how the parts fit together.","Initiation","Analyst")
